Im somewhat disinclined to agree with this point.  By the time you
get to the late game
  (1) you know what things do
  (2) you should be prepared

While Im sure its possible to get to Orcus with neither magic resistance nor
reflection, I have a feeling its Very Hard to do-- you learn about the time
that you meet the first thing with a death ray that if you dont have these,
you die quickly-- I just about always run into something with them well
before the castle..

Pretty much the only "new" stuff that you have to find out how to deal with
would be
  - not being able to pray [killed me the first time i got to the VoTD]
  - major demons, arch liches, etc.. fighting your quest nemesis should
    have taught you something about how they t'port to the up stair cases,
    you should know about Elbereth by now, and really about the only
    surprise might be Demogorgon, since hes the first monster (in vanilla)
    that can make you deathly ill [he killed me on my first time into 
    Gehenom proper]
  - Rodney-- who, besides coming back, doesnt really do anything that
    you wont have seen by the time you get to him, so hes not soo bad 
  - the invocation stuff, and vibrating square-- if you arent spoiled,
    it may take a bit to figure it out, but it wont kill you
  - the planes-- of which, only Air really gives you a "surprise" in that
    you need to figure out to levitate/fly, but that should be pretty
    straightward.. the astral has the rider monsters, which while new,
    their names say it all, and by then you should be pretty tough...

I dunno- Ive only died past Medusa's level a few times- my first
time in the VoTD, the first time I met Demogorgan, and once on the plane
of earth while trying to do a slashem extinctionist (mobbed by solars)...

